WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.603
-Clearly, you have to feel
the love from this crowd.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.137
[ Cheers and applause ]
-We do.

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:07.140
-We love you all!

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.408
-Guys, welcome to the show.

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:11.244
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.678
And I want to say, first of all,

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:14.446
congrats on
the Emmy nominations.

00:00:14.446 --> 00:00:16.249
-Thank you.
-Six. Well done.

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:18.885
-Seven.
-Seven. He's got one on his own.

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:21.854
-You got one on your own,
as well. Look at you. Wow.

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:23.756
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:25.925
-Thank you.
-It's just a great show.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:28.962
And I want to say before we even
go on to the interview --

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:31.798
But what you do for the people
on your show

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.933
and kind of making
their lives over,

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.035
it's one thing,
and it's beautiful.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:37.703
And if you haven't seen
the show, you should watch.

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:39.305
But, also, I just want to say

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.774
it also affects everyone
watching the show.

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:42.875
-Yeah.
-Thank you.

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:45.044
-And really, I --
I'll go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:47.146
Everybody's like,
"You're gonna cry."

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:49.516
I put it on,
and I'm just, like, weeping.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:52.718
I'm like -- I'm just so --
'Cause you're just so positive,

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:55.488
and you just go -- it just --
it comes through.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.757
And it's really genuine
and just --

00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:00.126
It's smart,
and it's good television.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.628
-Thank you.
-It's really great.

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:04.197
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.503
-I want to just go back
a little bit

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:14.807
and just see if there's any hair
or fashion or style choices

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:16.842
that you've made mistakes
in the past.

00:01:16.842 --> 00:01:20.012
I have some photos I want
to show you, just so...

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:21.914
-Oh, yes.
-Oh, please be Bieber.

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:23.983
Please be the Bieber look.
Oh, no.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:26.318
-Tan. You had a haircut
that you tried out.

00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:28.354
-I did. I will --
-This works for you.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:31.791
-Thank you. And so I wasn't
always known for my hair.

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:34.360
-I think you were, though.
-Leave me alone.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.830
That is so mean.
You are so vile.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.532
So vile.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.800
Here's the thing. Like, I --

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.269
I like to believe that
I started a certain trend

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:46.072
and then this megastar
decided to copy me.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.841
-You're telling me --
-You'll see what I mean.

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:51.010
-You're telling me that you had
a Bieber cut before Bieber?

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.713
-He didn't realize it was me
who inspired him.

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.448
-Early Bieber.
-Early Bieber.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.183
-Early Bieber.
-Yeah.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:59.719
-He was giving that --
-Oh, yes!

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.387
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes!

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:04.190
-Tan, that is
the worst thing ever!

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.226
-What you don't see
is the white leather belt

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:07.894
that he was wearing
with that look.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.128
-Oh, really?
-And the fist pump.

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:10.763
And the fist pump.
-Wait. No. Wait, wait, wait.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:13.299
-I like the fist pump.
-Look how pretty I look!

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.834
-Oh, my God.
-Beautiful.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.003
-Bobby --
-Adorable. You are adorable.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:20.206
-Bobby, your regrettable...

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.108
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.810
...fashion faux pas
was from actually --.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.646
-Yeah, it was just like
a year ago, I think.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:30.216
-Walk me through it.
-Um, well --

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.951
-That was before
I got to your color.

00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:33.753
That was before
I got to your color.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.320
-You know, there was
a very specific look, I think,

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.190
that producers in the beginning
had in mind for me.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.824
I think -- They're like --
Lies!

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:40.259
-..."He's the blonde one.

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:42.529
He should dress like Carson
dressed in the original."

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:44.930
It worked for Carson.
-You liked --

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.198
You liked wearing clothes

00:02:46.198 --> 00:02:47.867
that were the same color
as your skin.

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:50.236
It was lovely.
-You know, and in my defense,

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:53.706
it was also like 108 in the
summer in Georgia on that day.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.575
-I don't think it's --
-Can I just say? Can I just say?

00:02:56.575 --> 00:02:58.544
-Yes.
-Like, Bobby, our journey

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:02.481
together and hair color
has been amazing, I feel.

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:05.518
Because wow. The most improved.
-This is natural.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.286
-I know. Most improved look.
So beautiful.

00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:08.821
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:11.456
-"Our journey together."

00:03:11.456 --> 00:03:13.225
Karamo.
-Yeah?

00:03:13.225 --> 00:03:16.796
-You think you're --
You had a -- You wore --

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.363
-Yeah.
-Oversized clothes?

00:03:18.363 --> 00:03:21.300
-Oversized clothes.
I mean, anybody who's a product

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.502
of the early 2000s,
listened to hip-hop,

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:26.338
your clothes were like
three times oversized.

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:28.708
And so --
-Let me see.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.676
-Yes!

00:03:30.676 --> 00:03:32.945
-It's not bad.
-It's back in style.

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:34.881
-I want that, honey.
-I don't mind it.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.449
-I'm into it.
-That's a good photo.

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:39.852
That's, like, legit,
a good photo.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:42.655
That's, like,
a really bad humble brag.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.490
-Shiver my timbers. Gorgeous.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.726
-"Shiver my timbers."
Oh, my God.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:51.364
Antoni, you had -- you had
an interesting hairstyle.

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.066
I had a lot of hair.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.934
I'm growing it out now again,
but it was -- anyway, yeah.

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.769
-No, it looks great.
But here's -- here's an old --

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.437
a nice photo of you.
-Aww!

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:01.139
-Wow.
-Oh, no!

00:04:01.139 --> 00:04:03.276
-My face was a circle.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.344
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:06.111
-You couldn't even see anything.

00:04:06.111 --> 00:04:07.880
-Yeah, I was very round.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.749
I partied a lot in my early 20s.

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:10.883
-Oh, you look good.
-Yeah.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.151
-Who's that girl?

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.919
-It starts with the floppy hair.
It was really cute.

00:04:13.919 --> 00:04:15.054
-It's really
Ashton Kutcher-esque.

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:16.088
-Yeah. Definitely.
-There you go.

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:17.523
-Yeah.
-Johnathan.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:19.759
Any -- Any mistakes?
-I -- You know, I just --

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:22.094
I've literally just been this,
like, beacon of personal style

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:23.529
and good decisions
my whole life.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:26.231
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]
So I don't have any --

00:04:26.231 --> 00:04:27.766
I don't, I don't, I don't.

00:04:27.766 --> 00:04:30.036
I wanted to participate,
but I didn't have -- I just --

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.204
You know,
there's no bad pictures.

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:32.371
-This must have been
so uncomfortable for you.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:33.739
-It was.
I was like, "Uh..."

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:35.741
-You did so perfect.
Yeah.

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:37.676
I want to talk about this,
'cause I was actually

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:40.846
gonna suggest to you guys, like,
you should go to Europe

00:04:40.846 --> 00:04:42.748
or do something, you know,
to do --

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:43.849
-We love Europe.
-Yeah.

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:46.853
-You do?
I mean, but then I found out

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:48.888
you filmed the show in Japan.
-Yeah.

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:50.523
-Yes.
-It's so magical.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.291
In my opinion, they're some of
the most incredible episodes

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:54.126
we've ever done.
-Really?

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:56.428
-It's because
our cultures are so different.

00:04:56.428 --> 00:04:58.764
And they're just the most
beautifully kind

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:00.532
and sweet and civil people.
-And organized!

00:05:00.532 --> 00:05:02.034
And on time.
And --

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:03.503
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:05.838
-It made my heart sing!
-Yeah, it is true.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.107
Bobby, you were in your element.
-Are you a big deal in Japan?

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:11.210
-No, nobody knew who we were,
which was kind of nice,

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:14.313
because with the show, now
people kind of know who we are,

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:15.948
so when we walk in,
they're like,

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:18.384
"Oh, Tan, dress me, and, Karamo,
don't make me cry!"

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:20.019
And so things like that,
and so --

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.254
-"Don't make me cry"?
-That's usually what I get.

00:05:22.254 --> 00:05:23.556
-Yeah.
-"Please don't make me cry."

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:24.990
-Dude, do people cry
when they run into you?

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.692
-Oh, my gosh.
Literally, people come up to me

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:28.794
on the street and immediately
they'll start crying.

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:30.662
And I'm like,
"Nice to meet you, too."

00:05:30.662 --> 00:05:31.864
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:33.299
-It's really sweet.
But I like it.

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:34.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.701
-Yeah, why not?
-Why not?

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:38.103
-I love every segment
of the show.

00:05:38.103 --> 00:05:40.273
Each one of you do a great job,

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:42.675
but Karamo,
while we're talking to you...

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:43.876
-Yeah?
-...is there anything

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:45.745
you can tell our audience
and like...?

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:47.046
'Cause you're, like --
You get in --

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:49.114
You're like therapy for --
-Yes.

00:05:49.114 --> 00:05:51.651
-And could you give us something
that we can go out on.

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:53.919
-Yes. Everyone, turn to your
neighbor and say, "Neighbor."

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:56.522
-Oh, he's doing it.
-Neighbor.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.724
-"I am loved."
-I am loved.

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:00.859
-"I am beauty."
-I am beauty.

00:06:00.859 --> 00:06:03.295
-"And I am worthy."
-And I am worthy.

00:06:03.295 --> 00:06:08.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:09.936
-I actually want to show a clip.

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:12.338
Here's the Fab Five
in season 4 of "Queer Eye."

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:13.573
Take a look.

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:16.475
-Can I teach y'all something?
So go like this.

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:18.577
Oh, y'all got it?

00:06:18.577 --> 00:06:20.179
Ay!

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:21.914
-Karamo's got rhythm.
He's got spirit.

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.048
-Ay!

00:06:23.048 --> 00:06:25.051
Now ay!
There you go.

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:27.653
-He's mayor of Rhythm Town.

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:29.221
My other sisters --

00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:31.657
-I was just gonna follow her.

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.993
-...are not mayors
of Rhythm Town.

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:35.495
-Five, six, seven, move!

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:36.862
One, two!

00:06:36.862 --> 00:06:38.430
♪♪

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:42.334
-Oh, oh, oh!
Whoa!

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:45.571
[ Cheers and applause ]
Don't ask me.

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.907
-More with the Fab Five
when we come back!

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:50.576
More "Tonight Show"
Come right back, everybody!

